    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d355">

                <pb facs="0807" n="779" xml:id="pg779"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.5/10–1954: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 355<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the
                        Embassy in France</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d355-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">top
                            secret<lb/>priority</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1954-10-19T20:56:00-05:00">October 19, 1954—8:56
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Tedul 1. Eyes only for Secretary to be delivered immediately upon arrival<anchor
                        n="2" xml:id="d355-f2"/> from Robertson. Had highly gratifying conversation
                    with Senator George. He will support you and agrees that in view all
                    circumstances negotiation treaty desirable move. In absence discussions with
                    other Democratic members committee said he of course could not speak for them
                    but in his opinion all would go along.</p>
                <p>[Here follows discussion pertaining to prospective Senate ratification of the
                    Manila Pact.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hoover</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d355-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d355-f1-content">
                <p>Drafted by Robertson.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d355-f2" n="2" xml:id="d355-f2-content">
                <p>Dulles was in Paris Oct. 20–23; see <ref target="#d350-f5">footnote 5, Document
                        350</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
